  "term": "AACS",
  "definition": "AACS refers to a cancer cell-therapy approach that uses a person’s own red blood cells, modified to carry specific antigens and an immune-activating substance so the body’s antigen-presenting cells take them up. This is intended to trigger a targeted immune attack against tumor cells expressing HPV16-related antigens.",
